! v0.74.x Stage 2.2b -- methanol geometry optimization in IEFPCM water
! using the analytical PCM gradient.  Tests:
!   - the full %job opt + %pcm_grad_method analytical pipeline through
!     the optimizer (optimize_rfo_internals worker),
!   - convergence at a 6-atom system (small enough for fast CI but
!     larger than 3-atom water; exercises the multi-atom da/dR loops),
!   - a meaningful PCM shift in the optimized C-O bond length vs vacuum
!     (small but non-zero -- PCM tightens the C-O bond by a few mA).
!
! Stage 2.2a (FD path) timed at ~ 7 s for this opt; Stage 2.2b
! (analytical) target is a single-digit-second range.
%method  HF
%basis   sto-3g
%job     opt
%solvent water
%pcm_grad_method analytical
%geom_maxiter 30
%geom angstrom
C   0.0473  -0.0029   0.0011
O   1.4256  -0.0023  -0.0033
H  -0.3550   1.0254  -0.0102
H  -0.3506  -0.5304  -0.8915
H  -0.3528  -0.5180   0.9008
H   1.7424   0.9099   0.0085
*end
